WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.832
Today’s lesson goal: Today’s lesson goal: declare typed variables in C sharp. Read input and convert numbers safely. Calculate totals people can understand.

2
00:00:12.682 --> 00:00:28.642
Declare with a type: Declare with a type. String customer name equals Sarah. Int quantity equals 3. Double price equals 9.99. The type tells C sharp what kind of box you are creating.

3
00:00:29.492 --> 00:00:42.332
Why types help beginners: Types help beginners. The compiler catches many mistakes early. You see what each value is meant to be. Names plus types document your intent.

4
00:00:43.182 --> 00:00:54.630
Worked example: greeting: Worked example: a greeting. Write a prompt. Read the line into a string name. Then write Hello name with string interpolation.

5
00:00:55.480 --> 00:01:10.576
Worked example: tax total: Worked example: a tax total. Read a line of text. Parse it with double dot Parse to get a number. Multiply by one point two. Print the total with clear wording.

6
00:01:11.426 --> 00:01:24.410
Common mistakes: Common mistakes: using the value before Parse succeeds. Forgetting that ReadLine returns text. Opening a single file instead of the whole project folder.

7
00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:41.484
Practice, then quiz: Practice, then quiz. Complete the Module 2 exercises in your console app. Compare with solutions after you try. Take the Module 2 quiz. Then continue in the written lesson.
